UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150946Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting NORMA 
 (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocation: Netherlands-based a
 rts-sector activity. No city or region restriction stated.\nAward: Maximum
  EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may not exceed EUR 150\,000
  and the applicant organisation's annual budget may not exceed EUR 500\,00
 0. At least 25 percent of the project budget must come from audience or bo
 x-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 wage norms of EUR 139 
 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Single project\, typically a production or concert series. Final report du
 e within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/
 norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emap-emare-media-art-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150946Z
DTSTART:20261106T123000Z
DTEND:20261106T130000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 14:00 CET: EMAP / EMARE: European Media Art Platform Resid
 encies 2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 06 Nov 2026 at 14:00 CET.\n\nThe European Media Art Plat
 form (EMAP/EMARE) is a network of leading European media-art organisations
  offering fully funded two-month production residencies for artists workin
 g with digital media\, including media art\, bio art and robotic art.\n\nO
 rganisation: European Media Art Platform (EMAP / EMARE)\nLocation: Two-mon
 th production residency at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, Fr
 ance\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, 
 Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland\nAward: EUR 
 4\,000 grant for the applying artist (including subsistence)\; EUR 2\,000 
 for a collaborating artist (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo)\; EUR 4\,000 proje
 ct budget\; accommodation provided by the host\; travel covered per EU cei
 lings\; access to technical facilities and media labs. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Two months\n\nMore: https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Two-month production residency at one of 15 host institutions acro
 ss Austria\, France\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Sloven
 ia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Pola
 nd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-art-projects-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150946Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Projects
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Projects scheme contributes to the co
 sts of realising a contemporary art project. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, cura
 tors\, critics\, publicists\, partnerships and organisations.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Stroom Den Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicant
 s from outside The Hague (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes pl
 ace in The Hague or otherwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hagu
 e artists must be registered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).\nAward:
  Maximum EUR 10\,000 per project\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per cal
 endar year. Requests above EUR 5\,000 require at least 30 percent co-finan
 cing of the total budget from third parties. Artist fees\, production and 
 communication costs are eligible\; Stroom endorses the kunstenaarshonorari
 um.nl fee guideline. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the gr
 ant remains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, with 80
  percent paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://
 www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-projects?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rojects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from outside The Hague
  (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in The Hague or othe
 rwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artists must be regist
 ered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-seed-grant-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150946Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Seed Grant\, Autumn 2026 round
DESCRIPTION:The Stokroos Seed Grant supports early-practice visual artists\
 , designers and craft practitioners in the Netherlands with an unrestricte
 d budget for a self-defined plan: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 
 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives. The plan must start at least 10 we
 eks after submission\, last no longer than a year\, and can take place any
 where in the world.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLocation: Applica
 nts must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Ca
 ribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the funded plan itself 
 can take place anywhere in the world.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\,
  EUR 7\,500 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives\, as an unrestricted co
 ntribution to a self-defined plan. No application fee.\nDuration: Funded p
 lan starts at least 10 weeks after submission and lasts up to one year\n\n
 More: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (i
 ncluding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the fund
 ed plan itself can take place anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:perform-europe-open-call-2026-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150946Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Perform Europe: Open Call 2026-2028 (cross-border touring
 )
DESCRIPTION:Perform Europe is the EU support scheme for cross-border tourin
 g and distribution of performing arts works across Creative Europe countri
 es. WHAT IT FUNDS: touring of completed performing arts works (all perform
 ing arts disciplines except live music and opera)\; it does NOT cover prod
 uction costs for new creations.\n\nOrganisation: Perform Europe (co-funded
  by Creative Europe\, European Union)\nLocation: Creative Europe countries
  (27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU participating countries). Each partne
 rship needs at least three partners from at least three Creative Europe co
 untries.\nAward: Three grant tiers: EUR 15\,000 (small)\, EUR 25\,000 (med
 ium) or EUR 55\,000 (large) per proposal\, plus top-ups of up to EUR 5\,00
 0 for sustainability and accessibility needs\; absolute maximum EUR 60\,00
 0 per proposal including top-ups. No application fee.\nDuration: Touring p
 rojects within the 2026-2028 Perform Europe cycle\n\nMore: https://culture
 .ec.europa.eu/funding/calls/open-call-of-perform-europe-2026-2028?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture.ec.europa.eu/funding/calls/open-call-of-perform-europe-
 2026-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Creative Europe countries (27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU part
 icipating countries). Each partnership needs at least three partners from 
 at least three Creative Europe countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:culture-moves-europe-mobility-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150946Z
DTSTART:20270430T212900Z
DTEND:20270430T215900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CEST: Culture Moves Europe: Call for Individual Mobi
 lity 2026-2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 30 Apr 2027 at 23:59 CEST.\n\nFlagship EU mobility grant
  for artists and cultural professionals: individual or group (up to 5 peop
 le) mobility to carry out an artistic or cultural project in another Creat
 ive Europe country\, with the support of an international partner of your 
 own choosing (an individual or an organisation). The project must follow 2
  of the 4 objectives: to learn\, to create\, to explore\, or to connect.\n
 \nOrganisation: Creative Europe (Culture Moves Europe)\, implemented by th
 e Goethe-Institut\nLocation: Creative Europe countries (incl. overseas cou
 ntries and territories and outermost regions)\; the project takes place in
  another Creative Europe country than your residence\nAward: EUR 85 per da
 y of project implementation\, plus travel allowance of EUR 400 (under 5\,0
 00 km) or EUR 800 (from 5\,000 km). Top-ups where applicable: green mobili
 ty EUR 400\, overseas countries and territories / outermost regions EUR 17
 5\, family EUR 200 per child under 18\, visa EUR 120. Accessibility suppor
 t: EUR 30 per day plus actual cost or fixed allowance for personal assista
 nce or sign language interpretation. No application fee.\nDuration: Projec
 t-based\n\nMore: https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-fo
 r-individual-mobility?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-for-individual-m
 obility?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Creative Europe countries (incl. overseas countries and territorie
 s and outermost regions)\; the project takes place in another Creative Eur
 ope country than your residence
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:timisoara-mobilities-cultural-professionals-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150946Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: City of Timisoara Project Centre: Mobilities for Cultural
  Professionals 2026
DESCRIPTION:Travel-grant programme for individual cultural-sector professio
 nals (artists included) funding mobilities to or from Timisoara\, national
  and international: residencies\, research trips\, festivals\, presentatio
 ns and professional development. Continuous intake until the budget is exh
 austed.\n\nOrganisation: Centrul de Proiecte al Municipiului Timisoara\nLo
 cation: Timisoara\, Romania. Mobility must be to or from Timisoara\; open 
 to Romanian and foreign nationals aged 18+ active in cultural professions.
 \nAward: Maximum RON 7\,500 per national mobility\; maximum RON 10\,000 pe
 r international mobility. Non-reimbursable\, with a required co-funding of
  at least 1% of the project budget. No application fee.\nDuration: Per mob
 ility\n\nMore: https://centruldeproiecte.ro/finantari/mobilities-for-cultu
 ral-professionals-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://centruldeproiecte.ro/finantari/mobilities-for-cultural-professi
 onals-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Timisoara\, Romania. Mobility must be to or from Timisoara\; open 
 to Romanian and foreign nationals aged 18+ active in cultural professions.
END:VEVENT
